#NEXUS

[ tschopp2012a_fig11: Diplodocoid Nelsen consensus with WinClada character dots on every branch, read with the image as it stands (root at the bottom). Diplodocoidea, Flagellicaudata, Dicraeosauridae, Diplodocidae and Diplodocinae, joined by grey leader lines to nodes with their support values, are kept as internal labels; leader lines with support values only ('100 [5]', '21 [1]', '12 [1]', '33 [1]') name no clade. One three-way node: Diplodocoidea (Limaysaurus, Amphicoelias and Flagellicaudata). 14 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children); 5 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Picked case (character marks on branches; not a sample, not for accuracy estimates). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only; the marks and their numbers are not encoded. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=14;
    TAXLABELS
        Omeisaurus
        Camarasaurus
        Limaysaurus_tessonei
        Amphicoelias_altus
        Suuwassea_emilieae
        Dicraeosaurus_hansemanni
        Amargasaurus_cazaui
        Supersaurus_vivianae
        Dinheirosaurus_lourinhanensis
        Apatosaurus
        Kaatedocus_siberi
        Tornieria_africana
        Diplodocus
        Barosaurus_lentus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE tschopp2012a_fig11 = [&R] (Omeisaurus,(Camarasaurus,(Limaysaurus_tessonei,Amphicoelias_altus,((Suuwassea_emilieae,(Dicraeosaurus_hansemanni,Amargasaurus_cazaui))Dicraeosauridae,((Supersaurus_vivianae,Dinheirosaurus_lourinhanensis),(Apatosaurus,(Kaatedocus_siberi,(Tornieria_africana,(Diplodocus,Barosaurus_lentus)))Diplodocinae))Diplodocidae)Flagellicaudata)Diplodocoidea));
END;
